Package: libgd3
Architecture: any
Multi-Arch: same
Section: libs
Pre-Depends: ${misc:Pre-Depends}
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         ${shlibs:Depends}
Description: GD Graphics Library
 GD is a graphics library. It allows your code to quickly draw images
 complete with lines, arcs, text, multiple colours, cut and paste from
 other images, flood fills, and write out the result as a PNG file.
 This is particularly useful in World Wide Web applications, where PNG is
 one of the formats accepted for inline images by most browsers.
 .
 This is the runtime package of the library. Unlike Debian's build, it is
 compiled without Xpm support and so pulls in no X11 library at all.

Package: libgd-dev
Architecture: any
Multi-Arch: same
Section: libdevel
Depends: libavif-dev,
         libfontconfig-dev,
         libfreetype-dev,
         libgd3 (= ${binary:Version}),
         libheif-dev,
         libimagequant-dev,
         libjpeg-dev,
         libpng-dev,
         libtiff-dev,
         libwebp-dev,
         libz-dev,
         ${misc:Depends}
Description: GD Graphics Library (development version)
 GD is a graphics library. It allows your code to quickly draw images
 complete with lines, arcs, text, multiple colours, cut and paste from
 other images, flood fills, and write out the result as a PNG file.
 This is particularly useful in World Wide Web applications, where PNG is
 one of the formats accepted for inline images by most browsers.
 .
 The full development version of the library. Unlike Debian's build, it is
 compiled without Xpm support, so libgd.pc does not require xpm.
